1. Put builders, builder-authored tests, and CLI reviewers behind a real OS boundary with a dedicated home, standalone clone, restricted network, and no owner secrets or live-control access.
2. Disable automatic merging until the exact prospective merge tree against a fixed `main` tip has been tested and reviewed; any change to `main` creates a new integration version.
3. Replace linked worktrees as the isolation claim. Builders must never share refs, config, hooks, or object storage with the real repository.
4. Create an immutable per-job artifact contract and reviewed-bundle record containing full base/tip/tree IDs, mode, manifest, renderer identity, and digest; verdicts must cite it.
5. Make the tester run a sterile checkout of the exact candidate and verify the Feature Acceptance Checklist in the running app. A unit-test log must not qualify as browser/app evidence.
6. Harden Git input: reject merge commits, gitlinks, symlinks, binaries, attributes/filter changes, executable-mode changes, hooks, and unsupported control files for the first release.
7. Make reviewers tool-less and parse a schema-constrained out-of-band verdict. Do not search arbitrary stdout for lines beginning with `PASS`.
8. Make the Claude-build review roster operationally reliable: reserve review/test capacity before building and provide a reliable non-Claude fallback. Fix retry reuse before budget checks.
9. Replace truncation with preflight refusal and, later, complete chunk-coverage review.
10. Store full commit IDs; validate fresh clean workspaces; forbid plain-directory fallback; snapshot the actual provider, resolved model, runner, and pinned CLI version.
